  "cautions": [
    "The public Form I headword نَجَا is normalized from the Quranic lemma and includes the surface form نَجَوْ.",
    "The Quranic Form II use in 10:92 is a preservation or leaving-safe construction and should not be reduced to an ordinary generic rescue gloss.",
    "The hamzated noun نَجْأَةٌ discussed in the lexical material is a separate item and is not assigned to the ن ج و root.",
    "An attributed interpretation of نَجَوْتُ فلانًا as ‘I tested his breath’ is not treated as an independent meaning because the discussion rejects its evidentiary basis and explains the verse as private speech instead."
  ],
  "unassigned_or_ambiguous_evidence": []
